This declarative pipeline example demonstrates how to structure a multi-stage build process in Jenkins, including building, testing, and deploying different parts of your project. By using caching and specifying agents for each stage, you can optimize your build process and ensure consistency across different environments. Adjust the example to fit your specific project requirements, and you'll be well on your way to more efficient and maintainable CI/CD processes.

